-- #577: SpreadCopiesBatched with 62 children of six messages each. Every
-- fold of a child record into a summary, and every spread of the model,
-- looked each property up by binary search in three sorted lists (the
-- site's, the summary's and its marks), and every copy edge into a
-- summary's var was checked against a list or the edge table. The walks now
-- find each property where the last one ended, and a copy remembers the
-- last edge of each end. This build was past the gates' instruction budget
-- before. The golden was written by the compiler before the change.
import Browser
import Html exposing (Html)
import Tea


type alias Child =
    a : Int
    b : Int
    c : Int


type ChildMsg
    = M1
    | M2
    | M3
    | M4
    | M5
    | M6


